            <ArticleTitle>[Problem of &quot;organic neuroses&quot; (data on functional disorders of cardiac activity)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>51-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Examination of 66 patients with FDCA admitted to the cardiological hospital enabled two types of bodily sensations to be distinguished: homonomous--similar in their manifestations to cardiac pathology (cardialgia+, hysterical cardialgia and heteronomous--foreign to painful sensations in pathology on the part of the heart (senestoalgias, senestopathies). It has been established that somatic mental disorders manifesting themselves by functional abnormalities in the visceral organs may form not only within the boundaries of psychogenic (neurotic reactions) but also by constitutional pathology (phases, developments). Two-dimensional diagnosis (including both nosological and syndromal qualification) is respectively adequate to the qualification of the disorders examined, with their attribution to the &quot;supranosological&quot; group of somatoform disorders.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
